# @vouchme/gateway — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit real values.
#
# There is no deployed VouchMe Subgraph for this task (deployments/worldchain-sepolia.json's own
# notes) — src/chain.ts reads World Chain Sepolia directly (VouchMeRegistry events +
# GenesisAnchorBook.getIsUserVerified) instead of querying one. Contract addresses and the
# deployment block come from deployments/worldchain-sepolia.json itself, not from env vars here.
# The ONLY required variable below is GATEWAY_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY.

# ── HTTP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8787
HOST=0.0.0.0

# ── Gateway signing key (EIP-191) — REQUIRED ────────────────────────────
# The gateway signs every CCIP-Read response so the on-chain resolver's
# resolveWithProof() can verify it via ecrecover. This key's address must
# match the signer configured on the L1Resolver contract. NEVER hardcode
# this in source — it is read from the environment only (see src/sign.ts).
GATEWAY_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# How long a signed response is valid for, in seconds. Kept short because
# the underlying data can change on every new block (World Chain Sepolia
# mints roughly every 1-2s) — see the chain-read cache TTL below.
GATEWAY_RESPONSE_TTL_SECONDS=30

# ── World Chain Sepolia (chainId 4801) — optional overrides ────────────
# Tenderly primary, Alchemy public fallback ONLY (Alchemy's public endpoint rate-limits hard) —
# see src/chain.ts's buildTransport(). Both have working defaults; only set these to point at a
# different RPC (e.g. your own funded key) during local development.
WORLDCHAIN_SEPOLIA_RPC=https://worldchain-sepolia.gateway.tenderly.co
WORLDCHAIN_SEPOLIA_RPC_FALLBACK=https://worldchain-sepolia.g.alchemy.com/public

# ── Caching ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How long a fetched live-chain graph is reused before the next resolution re-reads the chain
# (docs/04-ens.md §3.2's 5s convention).
GATEWAY_CHAIN_TTL_MS=5000
